WEBVTT

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.290
Cucumber!

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.740
Nice and thick, all bumpy, 
and so delicious!

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:17.860
How'd you get these?

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:19.580
I got them from Kawabata-kun.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:20.400
Really?

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.330
You know, I've been thinking 
about this for a while,

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:24.220
but what do you think about 
Kawabata-kun and Houman-san?

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:25.200
You think they're going out?

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.680
Hm? I thought they were just friends.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.940
Hmm, yeah...

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:30.980
Well...

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:31.930
Well?

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:37.930
I'm sorry, Kawabata-kun.

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:40.300
I can't move when it's time to hibernate.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:41.640
I don't mind.

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:44.590
I don't mind at all.

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:47.350
I guess he's tucked her in before.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:48.110
What?

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:50.570
You mean like this?

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:49.830
<i>We should sleep.</i>

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:50.570
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:53.680
When it's cold, he gently 
takes her in his arms...

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:57.200
Wow, you mean like this?!

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:56.390
<i>We should sleep.</i>

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:57.200
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:07.610
Houman 
sleeps 
here.

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:02.150
See ya. I'll come and get 
you at the start of spring.

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:03.850
Thanks.

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:06.830
And Kawabata-kun's right by her side
when it's time for her to wake up.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:10.310
Oh wow! Oh wow! Oh wow! Oh wow! Oh wow!

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:12.410
I didn't know they were so close!

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:14.660
Love takes so many forms!

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:15.950
Love, huh?

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:19.050
Speaking of which, I hear that 
dolphins mate quite often.

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:22.510
What does mate mean?

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:28.190
Mate!

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:39.330
<b>Muromi-san on the Shore</b>

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:39.330
<b>Episode 12
"Muromi-san and Different Forms of Love"</b>

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:02.660
Fireworks!

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:03.990
Works, works!

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:09.950
Firing tons of sparks into the air 
that vanish in an instant...

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:12.090
I wonder if they intend it to be 
a metaphor for themselves.

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:13.920
Fuji-san, there you go again...

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:17.510
You see it light up, but then it 
disappears before you realize it.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:21.100
The light that signals a beginning 
simultaneously signals an end.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.150
Just like the short life of a human.

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:23.930
Fuji-san...

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:25.640
Yeah, but...

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:29.100
But it's pretty, so who cares?

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:33.570
You're right. Very pretty.

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:34.660
Where are you directing that?

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:35.520
Huh?

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:38.980
But it's nice to sit back in 
a quiet place and watch

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:40.740
from afar as the fireworks go up.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.940
When you're at a local show, it's 
noisy from all the people,

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:46.230
and your neck hurts from 
looking up. It sucks.

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:49.200
There's always a lot of 
fireworks shows in Tokyo.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.240
Yeah?

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:51.600
Last year, Levia-san wanted to

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:53.960
go around to different 
firework shows. It was awful.

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:55.760
<i>Tokyo!</i>

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:58.500
When she got excited, she tried 
to shoot off her hellfire.

00:03:56.980 --> 00:04:02.680
<b>Hellfire</b>

00:03:56.980 --> 00:04:02.680
<b>The Hellfire Blaster</b>

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:02.680
She could turn the world to ash 
without even realizing it.

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:06.140
Levia-san should just go ahead 
and turn the land to ash.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.100
For the children of God,

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:13.170
it's obvious that they're incapable 
of turning the land into a paradise.

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:13.950
Fuji-san...

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:15.410
It's true.

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:17.980
They still haven't even 
started working together.

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:20.860
Humans...

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:23.820
They've only had civilization for 
a few thousand years at the most.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:26.120
They're still full of potential.

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:29.830
You're acting surprisingly mature today.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:31.770
I like the humans.

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:33.690
Any species that prospers too much is

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:36.600
always destined to eventually fall to ruin.

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:38.670
The humans will follow the same path.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:41.380
The humans are historically the first animals

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:43.220
to have gathered this much knowledge.

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:47.490
What do you hate so much about humans?

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:50.060
What?

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:52.710
Come on, Muromi-san. 
You haven't noticed?

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:55.410
She had the person she 
likes taken away by them.

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:57.550
She can't help but dislike them.

00:04:57.550 --> 00:04:58.630
The person she likes?

00:04:58.630 --> 00:04:59.220
Yeah.

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:01.280
You mean the person Fuji-san likes, right?

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:02.210
Yeah.

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:02.740
Really?!

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:05.640
She wants Muromi-san to pay 
more attention to her.

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:07.320
Stop it, Sumida-san!

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:14.170
You should have just said that earlier.

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:16.820
Fuji-san, I...

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:22.450
I...

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:31.360
...hate those big breasts of yours!

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:34.790
Stop! You're going to tear them 
off if you grab them so hard!

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:36.370
They'll tear off... they'll tear off...

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:38.350
They're gonna tear off!

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:41.510
I want to tear them off!

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:43.190
Look at them!

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:44.210
They're gonna rip!

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:44.860
Rip!

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:46.660
Rip!

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:49.820
I want to rip them off!

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:51.780
Off!

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:55.750
Off!

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:58.540
Hii-chan, don't look.

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:07.740
The climax, huh?

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:22.620
Sumida-san, am I weird?

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:25.300
Love and weird are two 
sides of the same coin.

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:28.450
I want to be on the 
other side of Muromi-san.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:29.450
<b>Love</b>

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:30.450
Muromi-san.

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:30.450
<b>Weird</b>

00:06:31.880 --> 00:06:35.000
So I was wondering if there's some sort of

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:37.830
medicine to restore a damaged 
tail to its former state.

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:41.810
Yours doesn't seem to be damaged at all.

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:45.080
It's not for me.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.000
Muromi, huh?

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:49.360
Even if her tail goes 
back to the way it was,

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:51.230
she'll just go back up on land 
and damage it again.

00:06:51.230 --> 00:06:52.020
But...

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:55.470
A girl has to take care 
of her body on her own.

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:03.860
If I wrap her tail in gauze, I 
think I can help safeguard it.

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:06.570
I want you to say something 
to Muromi-san, too.

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:09.390
What are you talking about?

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:14.740
I want you to help me get 
Muromi-san's beautiful tail back.

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:17.360
<i>Fuji-san!</i>

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:18.190
If we prevent it from rubbing 
up against land, it'll go back

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:19.870
to that beautiful tail it used to be.

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:23.370
I don't really know what 
a good tail looks like.

00:07:23.740 --> 00:07:26.310
Like I've said before, I think Muromi-san

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:28.370
has a different set of values than you do,

00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:30.360
so I think you should 
just leave her alone.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:33.930
I've given up on stopping Muromi-san 
from coming up onto land.

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:37.550
But I want her tail to stay pretty.

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:40.280
Yes, if you saw it, you'd 
understand immediately.

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:41.940
It's so divine, it would change your life.

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:43.650
They say the past is never as 
good as you think it was.

00:07:43.970 --> 00:07:45.650
Anyway, I'm not the one 
you should be saying this to.

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:48.040
You should just talk to her about it.

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:51.320
I can't do it.

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:59.920
I hate to say this, but Muromi-san 
would listen to you—

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:02.030
Devil Fish Blade!

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:10.960
You're trying to lead Takkun 
on again, aren't you?!

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:14.260
Don't suck there!

00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:18.180
You don't have to be so mean 
to her, do you, Muromi-san?

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:21.050
Fuji-san cares about you in her own way.

00:08:21.050 --> 00:08:23.260
I keep telling her to stay out of my business.

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:25.490
It's her own fault if she won't listen!

00:08:25.490 --> 00:08:28.600
And now she's trying 
to go behind my back!

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:31.710
Sigh.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:37.570
From what Fuji-san was saying, your 
tail used to be really pretty.

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:40.510
I kinda want to see what that looked like now.

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:43.020
It wasn't that big of a deal.

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:44.230
You don't need to see it.

00:08:44.230 --> 00:08:46.090
Your tail determines how pretty you are?

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:47.920
How old is that way of thinking?

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:49.210
What's important is inside, right?

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:50.840
You need to factor in how 
pretty your heart is!

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:53.920
<i>How pretty your heart is? 
Are you in any place to talk?</i>

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:56.280
But how you look is important, too!

00:08:56.280 --> 00:08:58.850
You're just wasting your tail.

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:03.830
Then how about you lose your 
tail for a little bit?

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:04.560
Huh?

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:07.000
You can experience for yourself that

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:08.940
a tail isn't really that necessary.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.520
Stop! No!

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:12.180
It won't really hurt, so stay still!

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:14.420
Muromi-san!

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:02.910
<i>This is embarrassing.</i>

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:19.930
<i>Is she really...</i>

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:25.810
<i>Is Muromi-san really...</i>

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:31.530
<i>...going to rip off my tail?</i>

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:35.690
<i>If she tears me apart, what... what...</i>

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:41.100
<i>What will become of me?!</i>

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:51.410
Stop it, Muromi-san.

00:10:51.410 --> 00:10:52.720
She doesn't want you to do that.

00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:54.960
Come on, Takkun. You're too serious.

00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:57.870
I wouldn't really rip it.

00:10:57.870 --> 00:10:59.300
I was just messing with her.

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:01.420
<b>Tee-hee.</b>

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:01.810
And you're supposed to have a pretty heart?

00:10:59.900 --> 00:11:01.830
<b>Mad</b>

00:11:01.810 --> 00:11:03.760
You looked like you were about to do it.

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:10.680
<i>Huh, that's weird.</i>

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:13.150
<i>I saved her, but she's glaring daggers at me.</i>

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:15.010
Muromi-san...

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:19.240
If you were the one to do it...

00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:21.820
I wouldn't mind.

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:35.750
All right, here we go!

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:39.470
Rock, paper, scissors...

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:41.430
Fuji-san!

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:43.290
Over here!

00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:44.800
Huh? Oneetan?

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:48.700
Oh, Fuji-san. Fancy seeing you here.

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:50.090
<b>Distance.</b>

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:50.100
We've grown further apart now!

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:51.460
God is dead!

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:52.710
What's wrong, Muromi-san?!

00:11:52.710 --> 00:11:54.920
Next episode is the last 
episode! There is no God!

00:11:54.920 --> 00:11:56.830
Can't help it. All things come to an end.

00:11:56.830 --> 00:11:57.510
You don't know that!

00:11:57.510 --> 00:11:59.740
What are you going to do if Azazel-san

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:01.170
keeps on going and Muromi ends?

00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:04.660
Next Time
"The Years Go By Muromi-san"

00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:02.110
Do?

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:04.660
I'll just have to become 
the god of a new world!
